cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Brawlhalla RL: Vision-Only Reinforcement Learning on a Commercial Fighting Game"
message: "If you use this software or its findings, please cite it."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Zbida
    given-names: Mohamed Amine
repository-code: "https://github.com/MA-Zbida/brawl_scratch"
url: "https://github.com/MA-Zbida/brawl_scratch"
abstract: >-
  A reinforcement learning agent for Brawlhalla trained from screen pixels alone,
  with no memory access, no game API and no emulator, on a single consumer laptop.
  Comprises a YOLO-based perception stack, a structured state representation with
  explicit provenance, horizontal canonicalisation for sample efficiency, and a
  goal-conditioned skill curriculum with measured retention gates.
keywords:
  - reinforcement-learning
  - computer-vision
  - object-detection
  - goal-conditioned-rl
  - fighting-games
license: MIT
